 "known_issues": [
  "When two or more gauges on one river qualify for a river warning and no H-VTEC is cached, all are linked; backend-flood-live's background product-text fetch (nws.product_hvtec) makes it exact.",
  "rfc_max_forecast has no last forecast step: in the list, a forecast whose minimum comes before its maximum is read as 'still rising at the end' (conservative). The detail routes (NWPS series) decide exactly.",
  "Coastal tide gauges that NWS puts at minor are listed as river floods (PLAN-5 D1) and named after the nearest place ('Key Largo flood (FL)', 'Key Largo flood (FL, 2)').",
  "Two separate areal warnings along the same river in one state get numbered names ('San Juan River flood (UT, 2)').",
  "Past floods (mode=historical) answer an empty list with 'Fire-3d does not list past floods yet. That is not an all-clear.' until backend-flood-live M2.",
  "/api/floods/status is computed from the cached list until the flood live loop exists (backend-flood-live M1).",
  "The EARTHDATA_TOKEN path is untested with a real token (no token here): fake token + mock transport only.",
  "The fixture's canned answers keep the times of the run that wrote them; run make_fixture.py --only flood again to bring them to the present.",
  "The list build holds the catalog lock while its five requests run (up to ~30 s each on a slow source); concurrent callers wait for it."
 ],
